26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Or maybe this is the tightening we always needed.  Wheat from the chaff, etc. etc.</p><p>They always said pain plus reflection equals progress.</p><p>What they left out of the equation was time. </p><p>Cause we\u2019re all on a burndown clock to eternity.    </p><p>Which means your rate of progress is defined by the rate at which you can experience and understand <a href=\"https://campbellramble.substack.com/p/two-a-days\">pain</a>.</p><p>Aka the rate at which any machine learns, is the the speed at which that machine adapts, learns, in changes based on changes in conditions.  Particularly painful ones.</p><p>Looking a little closer to home, it looks like the conditions are changing.  Note the deterioration in economic conditions in the west below, as tightening sets in.  </p><p>Will we get a recession?</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cAs1!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F28d0f673-c5b1-43ff-9